@meta (title: "Estimate a documentation review", locale: "en-US")
@let minutes_per_page = 3
@let discussion_minutes = 15

# Estimate a documentation review

This fictional planning example assumes three minutes per page and an optional
15-minute discussion. It is an estimate, not a measurement of reading speed.

@slider pages = 10 (min: 0, max: 40, step: 1, label: "Pages to review")
@toggle discussion = false (label: "Include discussion")
@calc minutes = pages * minutes_per_page + if(discussion, discussion_minutes, 0)

Allow **{{ minutes }} minutes** for the current plan.

@when minutes > 60
Split this review into shorter sessions.
@end

@when minutes == 0
No reading or discussion is scheduled.
@end

@details "What this estimate leaves out"
Complexity, interruptions, and time spent making edits are not included.
@end
